        <class name="SortableBox" href="sortablebox.html" status="active" access="public" location="concepts.h" documented="true" module="Cpp20Concepts" brief="A box holding any Sortable type">
            <description>
                <brief>A box holding any Sortable type.</brief>
                <para>
                    <link raw="SortableBox" href="sortablebox.html" type="class">SortableBox</link> demonstrates the direct concept-on-template-parameter form with a namespaced concept: the parameter <argument>T</argument> is constrained by <teletype type="highlighted">traits::Sortable</teletype>, so the rendered class subtitle must resolve the fully-qualified concept name rather than the bare <teletype type="highlighted">Sortable</teletype> token.</para>
            </description>
        </class>
    </document>
</WebXML>
